id: pm-b0v8fs
title: "Read-output session receipts can emit an invalid next_state after the served-item set crosses its own 10,000-ID input ceiling"
description: "The strict static calibration now reproduces a caller-carried output session whose generated receipt contains more than PM_READ_OUTPUT_SESSION_MAX_SEEN_ITEM_IDS identities. parseReadOutputSession correctly refuses that state on the next read, so pm emits a next_state its own SDK and CLI cannot consume. The output-session producer must preserve already-carried identities, retain new identities only up to capacity, and disclose every newly delivered identity that could not be retained without relaxing the input safety ceiling."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-12T03:06:07.142Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-12T04:37:03.463Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-12T03:58:33.050Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-12T03:58:33.050Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Every emitted read_session.next_state is accepted by parseReadOutputSession; existing seen identities are retained monotonically; newly delivered identities are retained deterministically up to the 10,000-ID capacity; overflow is explicitly receipted instead of silently omitted; normal below-capacity envelopes remain byte-compatible; the real 2/2,243-item context calibration and all strict gates pass"
parent: pm-4k6b
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Read-session receipts preserve existing identities, retain newly served identities deterministically up to the 10,000-ID ceiling, and disclose overflow without emitting an invalid continuation."
expected_result: Every emitted next_state is valid input to the next CLI or SDK call while below-capacity output remains compatible and overflow is explicit.
actual_result: "Merged PR #986 adds optional seen_item_overflow_count across every SDK entrypoint; focused, calibration, full-coverage, hosted, and real CLI reuse tests pass."
